            {
                "entry_id": "47383d6e-50c1-3307-8096-e3fb32832c66",
                "word": "pentagram",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6d30a998-ae09-4c65-90b3-ef427450775f",
                        "entry_id": "47383d6e-50c1-3307-8096-e3fb32832c66",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pentagrams"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e27807a9-b560-38a7-ab30-d68578f3464b",
                        "entry_id": "47383d6e-50c1-3307-8096-e3fb32832c66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The shape of a five-pointed star constructed of five intersecting lines meeting at the vertices, such that a central pentagon and five surrounding isosceles triangles are formed; often with magical connotations; a 5/2 (or 5/3) star polygon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "268ef499-10ea-4007-8368-01a8bead3b7f",
                                "sense_id": "e27807a9-b560-38a7-ab30-d68578f3464b",
                                "text": "Prove that the circles so belonging to the 6 pentagrams formed by 6 lines meet in a point, and so on; the series of theorems being interminable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d057fa8-b2ec-49d8-a423-9d04a6a11c22",
                                "sense_id": "e27807a9-b560-38a7-ab30-d68578f3464b",
                                "text": "The passive pentagrams of spirit are drawn first in the quarters of the passive elements—water and earth—and likewise followed by the appropriate traditional elemental pentagram."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4b130c2-8d2b-4adb-a83d-58f3a4380799",
                                "sense_id": "e27807a9-b560-38a7-ab30-d68578f3464b",
                                "text": "Four figures involve 12 pentagrams arranged as in the faces of a dodecahedron with their vertices touching."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "acc1a083-fdd3-4fa4-8196-d60d84337d8c",
                        "source_entry_id": "47383d6e-50c1-3307-8096-e3fb32832c66",
                        "source_sense_id": "e27807a9-b560-38a7-ab30-d68578f3464b",
